avy fundraising advantage, and prediction markets all point the same direction, and the most recent polls show Risch comfortably ahead in a state that leans Republican by 18 points. The handful of outlier surveys putting Achilles close are contradicted by the weight of the recent evidence.", "watch": "If outside Democratic spending materializes as warned and consolidates behind Achilles, or if the divergent polls begin converging on a closer race, the margin could tighten.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Jim Risch (R) is running.", "Todd Achilles is an independent standing in for the Democratic side."]}, "overview": "Idaho is one of the most Republican states in the country, and Senator Jim Risch is seeking another term with the advantages of incumbency and a large financial edge. He has raised about $3.4 million and holds $3.5 million on hand, while independent challenger Todd Achilles has raised under $700,000 with little cash remaining. Every major race rating, ten in all, places the contest in the Safe or Solid Republican column, and prediction markets give Risch roughly a 96 to 97 percent chance of winning.\n\nThe polling record is unusually scattered: some surveys show Risch leading by 25 to 48 points, while a few others put Achilles close or ahead. Most recent polls point to a comfortable Risch lead in the mid-teens. Achilles, who says he would not caucus with either party, has drawn union support and highlighted the Iran war and living costs, but has not changed the race's fundamental shape.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0267, "margin": -10.92}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0421, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0262, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0261, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0155, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0312, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0381, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.01, "ma